test-backend-ops: GGML_TEST_KQ_SHAPES=1 runs only a decoder's two attention products over an F16 KV cache

The K-side product (a = the K cache view [head dim, keys, heads] and b = the
queries [head dim, tokens, heads], both permuted {0,2,1,3}) and the V-side
one (a = the transposed V cache view [keys, head dim, heads] with the cache's
row stride, b = the probabilities), at the key counts 1..256 and token counts
1..64 a small batch of sequences reaches, for 16 heads of 128 (T5/MADLAD-400).
A reproducer for an Intel Arc Pro B70 (SYCL, GGML_SYCL_F16) on which the
decoded text is wrong whenever two or more sequences decode together, right
alone and on the CPU, right again with an f32 K cache; the diagnostic build
(0005-llama-cpp-sycl-cpu-ops-diag.patch) named the K-side product
(2026-10-28). Run: GGML_TEST_KQ_SHAPES=1 test-backend-ops test -b SYCL0 -o MUL_MAT

diff --git a/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp b/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
index 8826b274b..e1dda3b44 100644
